sequenceDiagram
    %% Full maintenance workflow: submission → agents → approval → safety → dispatch
    %% Trust boundary: Browser and all data it supplies are UNTRUSTED.
    %% AgentRuntime prefixes every system message with UNTRUSTED DATA label on user/retrieved content.

    actor User as 👤 User (Technician / Supervisor)
    participant UI as Angular UI<br/>(untrusted browser)
    participant API as ASP.NET Core API<br/>(authenticated)
    participant PG as PostgreSQL<br/>(operations schema)
    participant Worker as Background Worker<br/>(lease-based)
    participant Orch as MaintenanceOrchestrator<br/>(Sequential Pipeline)
    participant SM as SymptomMatcherAgent
    participant RAG as RetrievalService<br/>(pgvector hybrid)
    participant LLM as LLM Provider<br/>(OpenAI / Ollama / Demo)
    participant DSP as DiagnosticSafetyPlannerAgent
    participant Safety as ISafetyPolicy<br/>(deterministic)
    participant WOG as WorkOrderGeneratorAgent
    participant Trace as WorkflowTrace /<br/>RunTraceStore

    %% ── 1. Job submission ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
    User->>UI: Enter symptom, select equipment
    UI->>API: POST /api/jobs {equipmentId, symptom}<br/>Idempotency-Key: <uuid>
    API->>API: Authenticate bearer token<br/>Validate equipment scope
    API->>PG: INSERT reasoning_jobs (Queued)<br/>INSERT reasoning_job_attempts (attempt 1)
    API-->>UI: 202 Accepted {jobId}
    UI->>API: GET /api/jobs/{jobId}/events (SSE)
    Note over UI,API: SSE stream stays open for live progress.<br/>Disconnect does NOT cancel the durable job.

    %% ── 2. Worker claims job ───────────────────────────────────────────────
    Worker->>PG: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED<br/>(claim lease on available job)
    PG-->>Worker: Job payload + lease token
    Worker->>PG: UPDATE reasoning_jobs SET status=Running, lease_token, lease_until
    Worker->>Trace: Start trace (execution_id)
    Worker->>PG: INSERT reasoning_job_events (WorkflowStarted)
    API-->>UI: SSE: {kind:WorkflowStarted}

    %% ── 3. SymptomMatcher ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Worker->>Orch: ExecuteAsync(request)
    Orch->>Trace: Start step (Agent, SymptomMatcher)
    Orch->>SM: MatchAsync(input)
    Worker->>PG: INSERT reasoning_job_events (AgentStarted: SymptomMatcher)
    API-->>UI: SSE: {kind:AgentStarted, agent:SymptomMatcher}

    loop retrieve_evidence tool calls (bounded by ReasoningLimits.ToolCalls)
        SM->>LLM: CompleteWithToolsAsync<br/>[System: prompt-v1 + UNTRUSTED DATA policy]<br/>[User: symptom + candidates]
        LLM-->>SM: ToolCall {name:retrieve_evidence, candidate:0, query:"..."}
        SM->>RAG: RetrieveAsync(query, topK, documentId, revisionId, Hybrid)
        RAG->>PG: Hybrid RRF query<br/>(keyword tsvector + cosine vector)
        PG-->>RAG: chunks {locator, snippet, embedding}
        RAG-->>SM: RetrievalResult[] (provenance-validated)
        SM->>LLM: ToolResult (evidence catalog JSON)<br/>Note: retrieved text marked UNTRUSTED DATA
    end

    LLM-->>SM: Final JSON {outcome:Success, candidate, symptoms:[...]}
    SM-->>Orch: SymptomMatchResult.Success
    Orch->>Trace: End step (Completed)
    Worker->>PG: INSERT reasoning_job_events (AgentCompleted: SymptomMatcher)
    API-->>UI: SSE: {kind:AgentCompleted, agent:SymptomMatcher}

    %% ── 4. DiagnosticSafetyPlanner ────────────────────────────────────────
    Orch->>DSP: PlanAsync(input)
    Worker->>PG: INSERT reasoning_job_events (AgentStarted: DiagnosticSafetyPlanner)
    API-->>UI: SSE: {kind:AgentStarted, agent:DiagnosticSafetyPlanner}

    DSP->>LLM: CompleteWithToolsAsync<br/>[No tools — evidence already in input]<br/>[User: symptom + match + evidence catalog]
    LLM-->>DSP: JSON {outcome:Success, steps:[...], prerequisites:[...]}
    DSP-->>Orch: DiagnosticPlanResult.Success

    Orch->>Trace: End step (Completed)
    Worker->>PG: INSERT reasoning_job_events (AgentCompleted: DiagnosticSafetyPlanner)
    API-->>UI: SSE: {kind:AgentCompleted, agent:DiagnosticSafetyPlanner}

    %% ── 5. Deterministic safety assessment #1 ─────────────────────────────
    Orch->>Safety: AssessAsync(plan, null)
    Note over Safety: Pure code — no LLM call.<br/>Reads reviewed-procedures.json.
    Safety-->>Orch: SafetyAssessment {canProceed, requirements}
    Orch->>Trace: End step (Tool: deterministic_safety_policy)
    Worker->>PG: INSERT reasoning_job_events (SafetyEvaluated)
    API-->>UI: SSE: {kind:SafetyEvaluated, allowed:true}

    %% ── 6. WorkOrderGenerator ─────────────────────────────────────────────
    Orch->>WOG: GenerateAsync(input)
    Worker->>PG: INSERT reasoning_job_events (AgentStarted: WorkOrderGenerator)
    API-->>UI: SSE: {kind:AgentStarted, agent:WorkOrderGenerator}

    WOG->>LLM: CompleteWithToolsAsync<br/>[No tools — uses plan evidence]<br/>[User: symptom + plan + evidence catalog]
    LLM-->>WOG: JSON {outcome:Success, description:"...", actions:[...]}
    WOG-->>Orch: WorkOrderGenerationResult.Success

    Orch->>Trace: End step (Completed)
    Worker->>PG: INSERT reasoning_job_events (AgentCompleted: WorkOrderGenerator)
    API-->>UI: SSE: {kind:AgentCompleted, agent:WorkOrderGenerator}

    %% ── 7. Safety assessment #2 (re-check final scope) ───────────────────
    Orch->>Safety: AssessAsync(plan, proposal)
    Note over Safety: Re-validates that the generated work order<br/>does not expand scope beyond the validated plan.
    Safety-->>Orch: SafetyAssessment {canProceed, requirements}

    %% ── 8. Atomic publication ─────────────────────────────────────────────
    Orch->>PG: TryPublishReviewAsync<br/>(INSERT work_order, work_order_snapshots,<br/>requirements; UPDATE run→WaitingForApproval)<br/>Concurrency token fenced
    PG-->>Orch: Published
    Orch->>Trace: End root step
    Worker->>PG: INSERT reasoning_job_events (WorkOrderReady, WaitingForApproval)
    Worker->>PG: UPDATE reasoning_jobs SET status=Completed, release lease
    API-->>UI: SSE: {kind:WaitingForApproval, workOrderId}
    Note over UI,PG: Worker releases lease.<br/>No Worker or HTTP request stays alive during human review.

    %% ── 9. Human supervisor review ────────────────────────────────────────
    User->>UI: View work order, review safety requirements
    UI->>API: GET /api/work-orders/{id}
    API->>PG: SELECT work_order_snapshots, requirements, decisions
    PG-->>API: Work order state
    API-->>UI: Work order + requirements + current status

    alt Supervisor approves
        UI->>API: POST /api/work-orders/{id}/decisions<br/>{decision:Approve, target:{revision,token}}
        API->>API: Authenticate; check approve permission + equipment scope
        API->>PG: INSERT decisions (Approve); UPDATE snapshot status→Approved
        API-->>UI: 200 OK
    else Supervisor edits and approves
        UI->>API: POST /api/work-orders/{id}/edited-safety-preview
        API->>Safety: AssessAsync(editedContent)
        Safety-->>API: New requirements
        API-->>UI: 200 {canProceed, requirements}
        UI->>API: POST /api/work-orders/{id}/decisions<br/>{decision:EditAndApprove, editedContent, reviewedRequirements}
        API->>PG: INSERT decisions; UPDATE snapshot; reassess requirements
        API-->>UI: 200 OK
    else Supervisor rejects
        UI->>API: POST /api/work-orders/{id}/decisions {decision:Reject, target}
        API->>PG: INSERT decisions; UPDATE snapshot status→Rejected
        API-->>UI: 200 OK
    end

    %% ── 10. Safety verification ───────────────────────────────────────────
    User->>UI: Record physical safety observation
    UI->>API: POST /api/work-orders/{id}/verifications<br/>{prerequisiteId, evidence, satisfied:true}
    API->>API: Authenticate; check verify permission
    API->>PG: UPDATE requirements SET verified_by, verified_at, evidence, satisfied
    API-->>UI: 200 OK

    %% ── 11. Dispatch gate (both conditions enforced) ──────────────────────
    User->>UI: Dispatch work order
    UI->>API: POST /api/work-orders/{id}/dispatch {target}
    API->>API: Authenticate; check dispatch permission
    API->>PG: Recheck: approved=true AND all mandatory requirements satisfied=true
    Note over API,PG: Server-side enforcement — not LLM output.<br/>422 if either condition false.
    API->>PG: INSERT dispatch_attempts (Pending); reserve token
    API->>PG: Dispatch adapter writes to inbox table
    PG-->>API: dispatch_attempt_id, state:Confirmed
    API-->>UI: 200 {state:Confirmed, attemptId}

    %% ── 12. Usage and trace persistence ──────────────────────────────────
    Note over PG,Trace: Every LLM call records to operations.llm_usage<br/>(call_id, actor, equipment_id, correlation_id,<br/>provider, tokens, cost) via AccountedLlmProvider.<br/>Trace steps queryable at /api/traces/{executionId}.
